// test_bridge_v1_lowwater_gas.prm
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// LOW-WATER VARIANT of test_bridge_v1_gas.prm, identical in every other respect except
// liquidHeightFactor LOWERED from 2.862 to 2.0. Real velocity-field data from the baseline run (job
// 4060404) showed the arches are actually close to FULLY FLOODED at steady state, not just grazing
// their base as an earlier turn assumed: the undisturbed away-from-bridge level settles at Z=62.5,
// but right at the piers it piles up to Z=71.5 (a real, steady ~9 LU local damming effect from
// supercritical flow (Fr=1.31) squeezed through the openings) -- and 71.5 exceeds even the central
// arch's own crown (66), let alone the two outer arches' (61). So getting a genuinely PARTIAL free
// surface inside the arch tunnels (water visible inside, clear air above it, up to the crown) needs
// the WHOLE water column lowered, not raised, so that even with the same ~9 LU pile-up the resulting
// level lands inside the 56-61/66 range instead of blowing past it.
// liquidHeightFactor=2.0 -> liquidHeight=8.00194*2.0=16.004, absoluteLiquidHeight=floorHeight
// (33.122)+16.004=49.13 away from the bridge; with the same ~9 LU pile-up observed in the baseline
// run, the estimated near-bridge level lands around Z~58 -- inside every arch's springing-line-to-
// crown range (56-61 outer, 56-66 central). NOTE: this pile-up estimate is carried over from the
// baseline run's own regime and not re-derived for this lower water column, where the piers occupy a
// larger fraction of a shallower channel -- the actual resulting level is something to read off this
// run's own VTK data, not something guaranteed by this estimate; the number above is a reasoned
// starting point, same as every other estimated parameter this session, not a promise. Everything
// else (Re/Fr/We, PID target, piers, arches, timesteps=30000) unchanged from the baseline run --
// isolating water level as the one changed variable.
//
// FIRST TEST BRIDGE, v1: real fluid flow, standard canal domain (same
// <128,60,180> / cellsPerBlock <32,20,30> = 72-process convention as
// cylinder_two_pillars_gas.prm), NO floaters/debris yet, NOT the real bridge
// dimensions (Pont ferroviere, Rue Goffontaine, Trooz -- pier spacing ~8.9m,
// length ~31.7m) -- a scaled-down shakedown to prove the geometry technique
// before scaling up.
//
// CORRECTION from an earlier turn: I initially thought BodyBC only supported
// Cylinder/Sphere/Ellipsoid with no way to carve a hole. Checked
// src/geometry/bodies/BodyFromConfig.cpp directly (the actual "shape" keyword
// factory, not just BoundaryFromBody.impl.h's includes) and it supports much
// more: Box (AABB), and full boolean composition -- LogicalOR, LogicalAND,
// LogicalNOT -- recursively nestable via "first"/"second" sub-blocks. So both
// requested features are directly buildable:
//
// PIERS (2): "round ends with box in between" = a stadium/capsule shape, built
// as LogicalOR(LogicalOR(Cylinder_frontCap, Cylinder_backCap), Box_middle).
// Each pier spans the full domain height (Z=0..180), footprint 16 LU long (X)
// x 10 LU wide (Y): end-cap cylinders radius 5 at X=61 and X=67, connecting
// box X=61..67, Y=+-5 around the pier's Y-centre.
//   Pier 1: Y-centre 15 (box Y=10..20)
//   Pier 2: Y-centre 45 (box Y=40..50)
// Wall gaps 10 LU each side (Y=0..10, Y=50..60), inter-pier gap 20 LU (Y=20..40).
//
// ARCHES (3, one per span -- now matching the real bridge's 3 openings): each
// span gets its own solid spandrel/deck box MINUS a cylindrical tunnel (axis
// along X, the flow direction), same construction as the pier-carving trick,
// just sized to that span's own width. Built as
// LogicalAND(Box_deck, LogicalNOT(Cylinder_tunnel)) per span.
//
// KEY FIX (geometry bug caught and corrected): the tunnel cylinder must be
// centred at the box's BOTTOM edge (the springing line, Z=56), not its
// Z-midpoint. Centring at the midpoint makes the circle touch all 4 box edges
// at single POINTS -- a lens/vesica shape, near-zero width right at the water
// line and only open at mid-height, backwards for an arch. Centring at Z=56
// instead means LogicalAND's own clipping against the box's lower bound
// discards the circle's entire lower half for free (nothing below Z=56 to
// intersect anyway) -- what's left is exactly the upper half: full-width
// opening at the springing line, narrowing to a point at the crown. This is
// also the key to sizing EACH span's arch correctly without any new "half
// cylinder" shape: for a true semicircular half-pipe, radius = half that
// span's own Y-width -- the same construction just scales per span, no new
// primitive needed even though the outer spans are narrower than the central
// one.
//   Left arch:    Y=0..10  (width 10), radius 5,  crown Z=61
//   Central arch: Y=20..40 (width 20), radius 10, crown Z=66
//   Right arch:   Y=50..60 (width 10), radius 5,  crown Z=61
// All three deck boxes: X=56..72 (matching pier footprint), Z=56..76 (free
// surface up to deck top) -- the outer arches' shorter crowns leave a thicker
// solid "collar" above them before the deck (15 LU vs the central arch's 10),
// which is structurally realistic, not a flaw.
//
// Free surface: same domain (X=128) as the reference runs this session already
// established avgParticleDiameter=8.00194 for (liquidHeightFactor 2.862,
// floorHeightFactor 4.1393) -- liquidHeight=22.9, floorHeight=33.12, surface
// Z=56.02. No rescaling needed/risked here since this reuses the EXACT
// reference domain size, unlike the widened-domain saga from the sphere/pillar
// scenario earlier this session.
//
// No CylinderPillars/DEM block: no floaters exist in this test, so there is
// nothing to collide with the piers -- the LBM-only BodyBC geometry above is
// the entire solid representation needed here.
//
// Domain: <128, 60, 180> / cellsPerBlock <32, 20, 30> = 4x3x6 = 72 processes
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

BlockForestParameters
{
   cellsPerBlock                 < 32, 20, 30 >;
   periodicity                   < 1, 0, 0 >;
   loadSnapshot                  false;
   storeSnapshot                 true;
   snapshotFrequency             10000;
   snapshotBaseFolder            snapshots;
}

DomainParameters
{
   domainSize         <128, 60, 180>;
   wavePeriods        1;
   liquidHeightFactor 2.0;  // low-water variant -- see header note; away-baseline absoluteLiquidHeight~49.1
   floorHeightFactor  4.1393;
   initialAmplitude   0;
}

PIDParameters
{
   targetMeanVelocityMagnitude 0.02;
   proportionalGain            2e-4;
   derivativeGain              1e-6;
   integralGain                2e-4;
   maxRamp                     1e-4;
   minActuatingVariable        0;
   maxActuatingVariable        1e-3;
}

PhysicsParameters
{
   enableWetting     false;
   timesteps         30000;
   Re                3100;
   Fr                1.31;
   We                15.6188;
   useHardcodedUnits true;
   // no gravityOverride -- dynamically computed gravity
}

ParticleParameters
{
   inFileName spheres_out.dat;
   bedCopiesInX 1;
   bedCopiesInY 1;
   densityRatio 2.55;
   fixingHeightFactor 1.5;
   frictionCoefficient 0.5;
   restitutionCoefficient 0.97;
   numSubCycles 10;
   useLubricationCorrection true;
   useNoSlipParticles false;
   useParticleBed false;
}

// DEM bodies matching the BodyBC piers exactly (BodyBC is LBM-only -- floaters need a real mesa_pd
// body to collide with, and nothing else creates one). 4 cylinders (the piers' round end-caps,
// radius 5) + 2 boxes (the connecting box between them, halfExtents = half of X=61-67/Y=10-20-or-
// 40-50/Z=0-76). center Z is cosmetic (CylindricalBoundary is infinite along its axis).
CylinderPillars
{
   CylinderPillar { center < 61, 15, 38 >; radius 5; }
   CylinderPillar { center < 67, 15, 38 >; radius 5; }
   CylinderPillar { center < 61, 45, 38 >; radius 5; }
   CylinderPillar { center < 67, 45, 38 >; radius 5; }
}

Pillars
{
   Pillar { center < 64, 15, 38 >; halfExtents < 3, 5, 38 >; }
   Pillar { center < 64, 45, 38 >; halfExtents < 3, 5, 38 >; }
}

// One entry per arch, matching the BodyBC arch cylinders exactly (center Y/Z, radius, and the deck's
// own X-span 56-72). Not mesa_pd bodies -- consumed directly by ParticleKernels.h's
// ComputeTunnelContacts (see its class comment for why: DoubleCast can't give CylindricalBoundary a
// second, inside-out interpretation, since the pillars above already claim the outside-solid one).
ArchTunnels
{
   ArchTunnel { center < 0, 5, 56 >;  radius 5;  xMin 56; xMax 72; }  // left arch
   ArchTunnel { center < 0, 30, 56 >; radius 10; xMin 56; xMax 72; }  // central arch
   ArchTunnel { center < 0, 55, 56 >; radius 5;  xMin 56; xMax 72; }  // right arch
}

ModelParameters
{
   pdfReconstructionModel        OnlyMissing;
   pdfRefillingModel             EquilibriumRefilling;
   excessMassDistributionModel   EvenlyNewInterfaceFallbackLiquid;
   curvatureModel                FiniteDifferenceMethod;
   useSimpleMassExchange         false;
   cellConversionThreshold       1e-2;
   cellConversionForceThreshold  1e-1;
   useBognerReconstruction       true;
   usePass3Reresolution          true;
}

EvaluationParameters
{
   performanceLogFrequency 5000;
   evaluationFrequency     1000;
   baseFolderName          eval;
}

StabilityChecker
{
   checkFrequency 0;
   streamOutput   false;
   vtkOutput      true;
}

BoundaryParameters
{
   Border { direction T;  walldistance -1; NoSlip{} }
   Border { direction B;  walldistance -1; NoSlip{} }
   Border { direction N;  walldistance -1; NoSlip{} }
   Border { direction S;  walldistance -1; NoSlip{} }

   // Pier 1 (Y-centre 15): stadium shape = two round end-caps + a connecting box. Capped at Z=76
   // (the deck top), NOT the full domain height -- piers stop flush with the top of the bridge
   // instead of poking up into the open air above it.
   BodyBC
   {
      shape LogicalOR;
      first
      {
         shape LogicalOR;
         first  { shape Cylinder; min < 61, 15, 0 >; max < 61, 15, 76 >; radius 5; }
         second { shape Cylinder; min < 67, 15, 0 >; max < 67, 15, 76 >; radius 5; }
      }
      second { shape Box; min < 61, 10, 0 >; max < 67, 20, 76 >; }
      NoSlip{}
   }

   // Pier 2 (Y-centre 45): same stadium shape, same Z=76 cap
   BodyBC
   {
      shape LogicalOR;
      first
      {
         shape LogicalOR;
         first  { shape Cylinder; min < 61, 45, 0 >; max < 61, 45, 76 >; radius 5; }
         second { shape Cylinder; min < 67, 45, 0 >; max < 67, 45, 76 >; radius 5; }
      }
      second { shape Box; min < 61, 40, 0 >; max < 67, 50, 76 >; }
      NoSlip{}
   }

   // Left arch (wall-to-pier1 span, Y=0..10, width 10 -> radius 5): same construction as
   // the central arch, sized to its own span so the opening is a true semicircular
   // half-pipe (full width at the springing line Z=56, point at the crown Z=61).
   BodyBC
   {
      shape LogicalAND;
      first { shape Box; min < 56, 0, 56 >; max < 72, 10, 76 >; }
      second
      {
         shape LogicalNOT;
         first { shape Cylinder; min < 56, 5, 56 >; max < 72, 5, 56 >; radius 5; }
      }
      NoSlip{}
   }

   // Central arch (pier1-to-pier2 span, Y=20..40, width 20 -> radius 10): full width at
   // Z=56, crown at Z=66.
   BodyBC
   {
      shape LogicalAND;
      first { shape Box; min < 56, 20, 56 >; max < 72, 40, 76 >; }
      second
      {
         shape LogicalNOT;
         first { shape Cylinder; min < 56, 30, 56 >; max < 72, 30, 56 >; radius 10; }
      }
      NoSlip{}
   }

   // Right arch (pier2-to-wall span, Y=50..60, width 10 -> radius 5): mirrors the left arch.
   BodyBC
   {
      shape LogicalAND;
      first { shape Box; min < 56, 50, 56 >; max < 72, 60, 76 >; }
      second
      {
         shape LogicalNOT;
         first { shape Cylinder; min < 56, 55, 56 >; max < 72, 55, 56 >; radius 5; }
      }
      NoSlip{}
   }
}

MeshOutputParameters
{
   writeFrequency 0;
   baseFolder     mesh-out;
}

VTK
{
   fluid_field
   {
      writeFrequency       1000;
      ghostLayers          0;
      baseFolder           vtk-out;
      samplingResolution   1;
      useMPIIO false;

      writers
      {
         velocity;
         fill_level;
         mapped_flag;  // cell type per timestep: 1=liquid 2=interface 3=gas 4=noSlip 6=freeSlip/UBB
                       // 7=UBB-inflow 8=pressure 9=pressure-outflow 10=outlet (VtkWriter.h) -- lets
                       // the bridge geometry (piers/deck/arches, all NoSlip=4) be isolated directly
                       // in ParaView (Threshold filter on mapped_flag == 4), independent of the water.
      }

      CellBB_filter_0 { min < 0, 29, 0 >;  max < 128, 30, 150 >; }
      CellBB_filter_1 { min < 0, 0, 0 >;   max < 1, 60, 150 >; }
      CellBB_filter_2 { min < 0, 0, 0 >;   max < 128, 60, 150 >; }

      inclusion_filters
      {
         CellBB_filter_0;
         CellBB_filter_1;
         CellBB_filter_2;
      }

      before_functions { gas_cell_zero_setter; }
   }

   domain_decomposition
   {
      writeFrequency             10000000000;
      baseFolder                 vtk-out;
      outputDomainDecomposition  true;
   }
}
